From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_pr_fixes_use_quaran <>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:43:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] os/mm: Make the use-after-free report safe to emit

Two problems on the reporting path, both of which get worse as the
detector finds more.

The hex dump covered the whole chunk. The most likely victim of a stray
write is the large top of heap free chunk, and mm_dump_heap_region()
emits one line per 32 bytes, so a 128 KB chunk produced roughly 4096
console lines with the memory manager semaphore held. On a serial
console that is long enough to trip the watchdog, and in report only
mode it happened on a path meant to be recoverable. Bound the dump to
256 bytes. A smaller chunk is still shown in full so the bytes on
either side of the corruption stay visible, and the checked window is
always included even though it fits inside the bound with the default
poison size.

The pattern was also left corrupted after reporting. mm_realloc()
verifies both neighbours before deciding whether to consume either of
them, so a neighbour it does not consume stays on the free list still
damaged and every later realloc touching it reprints the same report.
Re-fill the window once the report has been printed, so a second report
means a genuinely new write. The repair is skipped under
CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF_PANIC, where the crash dump should show the
corrupting value.
---
 os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c b/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
index a5706630..c81418c9 100644
--- a/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
+++ b/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
@@ -30,6 +30,19 @@
 
 #include "mm_node.h"
 
+/****************************************************************************
+ * Pre-processor Definitions
+ ****************************************************************************/
+
+/* Upper bound on the hex dump printed when a corrupted chunk is found. A
+ * chunk smaller than this is dumped in full so that the bytes on either side
+ * of the corruption stay visible; a larger one is truncated. Without the
+ * bound, a corrupted top of heap chunk dumps the whole remaining heap, one
+ * line per 32 bytes, with the memory manager semaphore held.
+ */
+
+#define MM_UAF_DUMP_MAX		256
+
 /****************************************************************************
  * Private Functions
  ****************************************************************************/
@@ -129,6 +142,7 @@ void mm_uaf_verify(struct mm_freenode_s *node)
 {
 	uint32_t *poison;
 	size_t nwords;
+	size_t dumpsize;
 	size_t i;
 
 	nwords = mm_uaf_area(node, &poison);
@@ -144,12 +158,35 @@ void mm_uaf_verify(struct mm_freenode_s *node)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* Show the checked window whatever happens, plus as much of the rest of
+	 * the chunk as the bound allows.
+	 */
+
+	dumpsize = MM_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE) + nwords * sizeof(uint32_t);
+	if (dumpsize < MM_UAF_DUMP_MAX) {
+		dumpsize = MM_UAF_DUMP_MAX;
+	}
+
+	if (dumpsize > node->size) {
+		dumpsize = node->size;
+	}
+
 	heap_dbg("#########################################################################################\n");
 	mfdbg("ERROR: Use after free detected.\n");
 	mm_dump_node((struct mm_allocnode_s *)node, "FREE NODE");
-	mm_dump_heap_region((uint32_t)node, (uint32_t)node + node->size);
+	mm_dump_heap_region((uint32_t)node, (uint32_t)node + dumpsize);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF_PANIC
 	PANIC();
+#else
+	/* Repair the pattern now that the corruption has been reported.
+	 *
+	 * mm_realloc() verifies both neighbours before it decides whether to
+	 * consume either of them. A neighbour it does not consume stays on the
+	 * free list still corrupted, so without this repair every later realloc
+	 * touching it prints the same report again, forever, from one defect.
+	 */
+
+	mm_uaf_poison(node);
 #endif
 }
